### How do you define a custom annotation?

```java
import java.lang.annotation.*;

@Target(ElementType.METHOD)            // can only be on methods
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)    // available at runtime
@Documented                            // included in javadoc
public @interface Audited {
    String action() default "";         // optional element with default
    String description() default "";
}
```

### How do you use it?

```java
public class TransferService {

    @Audited(action = "TRANSFER", description = "Debit and credit between accounts")
    public void transfer(Account from, Account to, BigDecimal amount) {
        from.debit(amount);
        to.credit(amount);
    }
}
```

### How do you read it at runtime?

```java
Method method = TransferService.class.getMethod("transfer", Account.class, Account.class, BigDecimal.class);
if (method.isAnnotationPresent(Audited.class)) {
    Audited audit = method.getAnnotation(Audited.class);
    System.out.println("Action: " + audit.action());        // TRANSFER
    System.out.println("Desc: " + audit.description());     // Debit and credit...
}
```

### What element types are allowed?

Annotation elements can only be: primitives, String, Class, enums, other annotations, or arrays of these.

```java
public @interface Config {
    int maxRetries() default 3;                 // primitive
    String environment() default "PRODUCTION";  // String
    Class<?> handler() default Object.class;    // Class
    AccountType type() default AccountType.SAVINGS;  // enum
    Audited[] audits() default {};              // array of annotations
}
```

### What should a senior engineer know?

- **Spring AOP uses custom annotations** for cross-cutting concerns: `@Cacheable`, `@Retry`, `@RateLimited`.
- **Lombok** processes annotations at compile time to generate code (getters, builders).
- **AnnotationProcessor (JSR 269)** lets you generate source files during compilation. Used by MapStruct, Dagger.
- **@Repeatable** (Java 8+) allows multiple of the same annotation: `@Role("ADMIN") @Role("AUDITOR")`.
